      "body": "Working this on branch `fix/chat-mermaid-render`.\n\n**Verified live** via `dev:web` + headless Chromium (temp demo route, since removed): 3 diagrams render with zero page errors in both themes \u2014 chat flowchart, chat sequence diagram, and markdown file Preview \u2014 plus the invalid-syntax fallback to source with caption.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `frontend/src/renderer/lib/mermaid-diagram.ts` (new): lazy dynamic import of mermaid (chunk loads only when a diagram exists), `securityLevel: strict`, parse-before-render so syntax errors fall back instead of rendering error boxes, DOMPurify with `foreignObject` + its integration point added back (flowchart/state labels render as HTML inside it; DOMPurify's default integration points would empty every label) while `img`/`image`/media/form/script/active content stay forbidden, 20KB size cap, bounded SVG cache.\n- `frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/MermaidBlock.tsx` (new): diagram chrome matching code blocks (mermaid label, copy source, diagram/source toggle), plain-text-first loading, no render while streaming, source fallback with caption on failure, re-render on AO theme flip, link clicks intercepted into the chat external-link policy (never navigates the renderer).\n- Wired into `ChatMarkdown.tsx` (case-insensitive) and `MarkdownFileView.tsx`.\n\n**Checks:** `tsc --noEmit` clean; 470 tests pass across chat+markdown suites (11 new); real-engine Chromium check confirmed labels kept and `onerror`/`<script>`/`javascript:` URLs/label `<img>` all stripped.",
