    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Problem\n\n```mermaid fenced blocks in agent chat output render as plain monospace code, not as diagrams. Agents frequently emit architecture flows as mermaid (e.g. in plans/specs), so the reader gets source text instead of the picture.\n\n## Repro\n\n1. Have an agent emit (or paste into chat):\n```\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[User] --> B[AO]\n```\n```\n2. Observe the timeline shows a code block labeled \"mermaid\" with raw source, no diagram.\n\n## Root cause (checked on `main` @ 213dfe39)\n\n- `frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatMarkdown.tsx` routes every fence through `CodeBlock` -> `HighlightedCode`.\n- `frontend/src/renderer/lib/code-highlight.ts` `canonicalLanguage('mermaid')` returns `undefined`, so it renders plain monospace and loads no grammar.\n- No `mermaid` dependency in `frontend/package.json`; same path in `frontend/src/renderer/components/markdown/MarkdownFileView.tsx` (markdown file Preview tab).\n- Dedup: searched issues for `mermaid` / `diagram` / `markdown rendering`. Only hit is #4514, which merely embeds a mermaid flow in its own body as documentation, not a rendering bug. No existing rendering issue.\n\n## Expected\n\n- ```mermaid fences in chat render as SVG diagrams (with source fallback + copy), respecting light/dark theme and not breaking the existing no-raw-HTML sanitization story.\n- Same handling in markdown file Preview if cheap; at minimum chat.\n\n## Scope note\n\nRenderer CSP is `script-src 'self'` with no `wasm-unsafe-eval` (see `vite.renderer.config.ts`, `code-highlight.ts` header). Implementation must work within that (mermaid is plain JS, but its SVG output needs sanitized injection rather than the current token-tree-only path).",
